WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.769
[MUSIC]

00:00:07.769 --> 00:00:11.066
It's March in Mozambique.

00:00:11.066 --> 00:00:14.335
I'm wearing one of those one size fits all
safety vests and

00:00:14.335 --> 00:00:17.000
I have on my steel toed boots.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:21.170
I'm planted in front of a crowd of 20
dusty miners.

00:00:21.170 --> 00:00:23.060
We're in a hot, crowded conference room.

00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:26.030
As their equipment supplier,

00:00:26.030 --> 00:00:29.280
I've been invited to advise them on how
they might improve their operation.

00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:33.850
I captivate my audience with a warm smile
on my face.

00:00:35.550 --> 00:00:36.610
Is warmth a weakness?

00:00:38.170 --> 00:00:39.610
Just the opposite.

00:00:39.610 --> 00:00:41.899
With this crowd it is the secret to
success.

00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:47.900
Two days later, and I'm in a meeting in
Johannesburg with student executives.

00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:50.180
The assignment is the same but

00:00:50.180 --> 00:00:53.590
this time I command my audience with a
polished confidence.

00:00:55.130 --> 00:00:58.625
As a leader is it better to be respected
or liked?

00:01:00.220 --> 00:01:01.845
Powerful, or empathetic?

00:01:01.845 --> 00:01:06.880
Feared or loved?

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:10.920
In the year 1513 Machiavelli advocated for
fear over love.

00:01:12.030 --> 00:01:14.673
He also never had to face a 360 degree
review.

00:01:14.673 --> 00:01:15.330
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH].

00:01:15.330 --> 00:01:20.230
&gt;&gt; 500 years later I propose that we need
to

00:01:20.230 --> 00:01:24.080
be both respected and liked to be
effective leaders.

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:28.220
There appears to be a tension between
these attributes, but

00:01:28.220 --> 00:01:30.550
they are not mutually exclusive.

00:01:30.550 --> 00:01:34.350
Strength and warmth exist on a continuum.

00:01:34.350 --> 00:01:36.350
In both of the cases that I described,

00:01:36.350 --> 00:01:39.870
I was acting within the realm of my
authentic self.

00:01:39.870 --> 00:01:43.510
By knowing my audience I could fluidly
move along the continuum

00:01:43.510 --> 00:01:45.550
to a place that allowed me to be
influential.

00:01:46.970 --> 00:01:50.810
Though why these two qualities strength
and warmth anyway?

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:54.820
They are the two most important traits in
influencing your audience.

00:01:55.960 --> 00:02:01.270
In fact, the field of psychology credits
over 90% of the positive and

00:02:01.270 --> 00:02:06.120
negative impressions we form about others
back to strength and warmth.

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:10.670
Strength is confidence, credibility.

00:02:10.670 --> 00:02:11.313
Warmth?

00:02:11.313 --> 00:02:13.761
Approachability, kindness.

00:02:15.010 --> 00:02:18.190
When we judge someone these are the
qualities that we are looking at.

00:02:19.398 --> 00:02:22.740
We admire leaders who are fully using both
strength and

00:02:22.740 --> 00:02:24.360
warmth because we know it's not easy.

00:02:24.360 --> 00:02:26.532
There are things that get in a way,

00:02:26.532 --> 00:02:31.590
things that complicate our ability to
authentically engage strength and warmth.

00:02:31.590 --> 00:02:33.010
One of those things?

00:02:33.010 --> 00:02:33.510
Anxiety.

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:40.510
Standing here at the front of the room I
have the privilege of influencing how you,

00:02:40.510 --> 00:02:41.670
my audience, feels.

00:02:42.950 --> 00:02:48.500
Now this feels a bit stressful, so I have
extra testosterone, strength hormone.

00:02:48.500 --> 00:02:54.140
But this extra testosterone by definition
is inhibiting my oxytocin, warmth hormone.

00:02:55.330 --> 00:02:59.560
And if that's not enough, my cortisol is
high too because of stress and

00:02:59.560 --> 00:03:00.850
that's undermining my strength.

00:03:02.090 --> 00:03:06.940
To sum it up, feeling anxious and the
overwhelming chemistry that comes surging

00:03:06.940 --> 00:03:10.740
with it, won't allow me to project either
strength or warmth.

00:03:12.070 --> 00:03:15.960
We feel anxious in situations where we
wanna make a good impression.

00:03:15.960 --> 00:03:18.860
What we need to do though, is learn to
manage our anxiety.

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:24.135
Your best bet, the next time you're in a
stressful situation, like this?

00:03:24.135 --> 00:03:25.150
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH].

00:03:25.150 --> 00:03:27.440
&gt;&gt; Work with the chemistry.

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:29.040
Breathe and smile.

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:35.139
Both taking a deep breath and smiling will
help pair up your cortisone levels.

00:03:36.730 --> 00:03:39.640
We need to manage anxiety to use the
strength warmth

00:03:39.640 --> 00:03:41.690
continuum in the first place.

00:03:41.690 --> 00:03:43.510
But once we have that under control,

00:03:43.510 --> 00:03:46.200
how can we make our continuum as ample as
possible?

00:03:48.050 --> 00:03:53.000
Well, we need to extend ourselves to
cultivate the maximum amount of strength

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:54.930
and warmth as authentically possible.

00:03:56.480 --> 00:03:59.420
My career has been at a mature company.

00:03:59.420 --> 00:04:03.770
So mature in fact, that it will be
celebrating 90 years next month.

00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:08.270
And in my rather large division, about
4,000 people,

00:04:08.270 --> 00:04:10.970
I was the first woman to go to the field
and work in sales.

00:04:12.050 --> 00:04:14.880
And the only reason that I survived that
assignment,

00:04:14.880 --> 00:04:19.740
it's because I learned how to balance
strength and warmth and to dial up both

00:04:19.740 --> 00:04:23.010
to the maximum that I could while still
authentically being myself.

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:28.971
It all started when I choose Mining
Engineering on my university application.

00:04:28.971 --> 00:04:31.183
Who does that?

00:04:31.183 --> 00:04:36.715
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; Well not very many 17 year old girls.

00:04:36.715 --> 00:04:39.894
Female enrollment runs at just under 12%.

00:04:39.894 --> 00:04:43.085
I noticed, but it didn't bother me.

00:04:43.085 --> 00:04:47.130
My small, supportive cohort formed a
comfortable environment.

00:04:47.130 --> 00:04:48.070
I felt like I belonged.

00:04:48.070 --> 00:04:50.560
I felt completely free to be myself.

00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:53.400
And it turns out the time I spent in that
space,

00:04:53.400 --> 00:04:55.800
was really important to developing my
confidence.

00:04:56.840 --> 00:05:01.518
When I graduated from university, the
prospect of working in a male-dominated

00:05:01.518 --> 00:05:03.740
field, well I didn't see it as an issue at
all.

00:05:04.940 --> 00:05:09.610
I went on to work in mining machine sales
in South America.

00:05:09.610 --> 00:05:13.770
Think bright yellow truck the size of a
two story house that costs $6 million.

00:05:15.420 --> 00:05:19.410
If you're thinking that this space is
short on female role models, it is.

00:05:19.410 --> 00:05:23.260
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; In fact when my company offered me

00:05:23.260 --> 00:05:28.150
the position my boss shared with me that
not everybody supported my promotion.

00:05:28.150 --> 00:05:31.790
Many didn't believe that as a woman I
could be successful in that environment.

00:05:33.010 --> 00:05:34.460
I felt completely betrayed.

00:05:34.460 --> 00:05:38.870
I thought about all the chatter that was
going on around me about me.

00:05:38.870 --> 00:05:43.450
And I let my confidence get displaced by
self-doubt.

00:05:43.450 --> 00:05:48.600
But, as I started to organize my move from
Miami to Sao Paolo.

00:05:48.600 --> 00:05:49.400
I started to change.

00:05:50.400 --> 00:05:53.970
I made the intentional decision to
represent myself with

00:05:53.970 --> 00:05:56.070
all of the confidence and competence that
I had.

00:05:57.140 --> 00:05:59.850
And it was essential to control for
biases,

00:05:59.850 --> 00:06:05.140
like being a woman which was articulated
ever so clearly to me.

00:06:05.140 --> 00:06:10.220
But also for other biases that I hadn't
thought about, like being a foreigner or

00:06:10.220 --> 00:06:11.350
not having field experience.

00:06:12.360 --> 00:06:14.135
And one that probably all of us have
faced,

00:06:14.135 --> 00:06:15.940
being the youngest person in the room.

00:06:17.270 --> 00:06:21.210
Instead of suffering with these biases, I
developed a thick skin and moved forward.

00:06:22.560 --> 00:06:25.800
At the same time, though, I found a great
niche for myself,

00:06:25.800 --> 00:06:29.879
using warmth to its fullest potential and
in an aggressive competitive environment.

00:06:31.590 --> 00:06:36.130
Imagine you run into me at the world's
largest iron ore mine

00:06:36.130 --> 00:06:37.780
in the Amazon jungle.

00:06:37.780 --> 00:06:39.800
It's the rain forest so I'm drowning in
mud.

00:06:39.800 --> 00:06:40.980
I'll have on my rubber boots.

00:06:42.150 --> 00:06:45.090
In the distance you can see my bright
yellow hard hat

00:06:45.090 --> 00:06:48.670
with my blonde pony tail bouncing
underneath and a bright smile on my face.

00:06:50.720 --> 00:06:52.500
Now, my gender and

00:06:52.500 --> 00:06:57.245
this Scandinavian phenotype are not
especially common in the Amazon.

00:06:57.245 --> 00:06:59.760
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH].

00:06:59.760 --> 00:07:02.270
&gt;&gt; Much less in the pit of an iron ore
mine.

00:07:02.270 --> 00:07:06.460
I had the great opportunity to play
against type.

00:07:06.460 --> 00:07:10.300
The curiosity that it created was a means
to connect with people and

00:07:10.300 --> 00:07:11.089
build relationships.

00:07:12.700 --> 00:07:15.260
Well it sounds nice, to dial up strength
and

00:07:15.260 --> 00:07:17.840
warmth, to navigate challenging
situations.

00:07:17.840 --> 00:07:18.810
It's not always easy.

00:07:19.860 --> 00:07:20.940
Maybe, like me,

00:07:20.940 --> 00:07:24.780
you fail to find the confidence to speak
up in an important client meeting.

00:07:25.920 --> 00:07:27.070
Or in the same meeting,

00:07:27.070 --> 00:07:29.940
found it impossible to empathize with that
difficult client.

00:07:31.070 --> 00:07:32.730
If you find yourself missing one or

00:07:32.730 --> 00:07:35.620
the other, remember that they are not
mutually exclusive.

00:07:37.040 --> 00:07:41.710
When you feel composed and in control, you
can project comfort and warmth.

00:07:43.140 --> 00:07:45.370
After all, the overarching objective,

00:07:45.370 --> 00:07:50.300
as a leader, is not to simply control your
audience or to make them feel good.

00:07:50.300 --> 00:07:52.450
But to influence them.

00:07:52.450 --> 00:07:55.480
By managing our anxiety we've cleared the
first hurdle

00:07:55.480 --> 00:07:58.930
to using the strength form continuum.

00:07:58.930 --> 00:08:01.820
From there we can work on making it as
ample as possible.

00:08:01.820 --> 00:08:05.050
By maximizing the amount of strength and
warmth that we show.

00:08:06.410 --> 00:08:11.680
The next time you walk into a room,
whether you're facing dusty coal miners,

00:08:11.680 --> 00:08:15.440
suited executives or something else
entirely?

00:08:15.440 --> 00:08:21.207
Ask yourself the question how I will I
balance strength and warmth?

00:08:21.207 --> 00:08:21.868
Thank you.

00:08:21.868 --> 00:08:23.563
[APPLAUSE]

00:08:23.563 --> 00:08:27.849
[MUSIC]

